1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
The best way to start a speech and the way that I hope all of you use from now forward

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
is the same way we start a story to a child.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
But in business, you don't hear Jack Welsh saying once upon a time.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Steve Jobs doesn't start his speeches once upon a time.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
So there's a grown-up way of saying once upon a time.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
The way you tell stories as an adult is in October, it was the last time I was in this

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
room, there were 120 people in the room and I was having a little conversation with one

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
of the world experts on public speaking.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000
And he said something to me that's had me thinking ever since.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
He said something to me that changed what I think about what's important in speaking.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Now I can pause for about 30 seconds, two, three minutes.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
And you want to know what he said.

